 AVClass {'submitted': True, 'pending': []} AVClass is a static const class descriptor: every in-tree instance is a file-scope `static const AVClass` (or `const AVClass` exported) with designated initializers, reached as `const AVClass *` (first member of an AVClass-enabled object, *_get_class() returns, child_class_iterate results). No C path allocates, writes, copies or frees one (field touchers only read), so it has no lifecycle primitives; Rust wraps it as a borrowed ClassRef<'a> (getters only, the callbacks as callable handles), plus a const Rust constructor for Rust-owned static classes. Scalars: version (LIBAVUTIL_VERSION_INT at definition), offsets into the described object (0 = none), category by value.
