def submission(slug,value): write(pathlib.Path('wavefront')/slug/'submission.json',json.dumps(value,indent=2)+'\\n')
submission('helper-is-not-a-print-buffer',{'_comment_agent': 'Review core wave-1 batch-0: ff_pad_helper_AVBPrint is a sizeof-only witness generated by FF_PAD_STRUCTURE. No C path instantiates it, passes it to a bprint routine, owns its pointee, or disposes it. The authored BPrintFields value uses str only as a nullable borrowed immutable C string, with no relationship to len/size/size_max or reserved_internal_buffer. AVBPrint ownership belongs to the separate AVBPrint record, not this helper.', 'fields':{'str':{'ptr':{'scalar':None,'array':None,'string':True,'owned':False,'borrowed':{'lifetime':'other'},'nullable':True,'mutable':False,'note':'C uses this helper only in sizeof; it has no observed runtime pointer ownership. BPrintFields in the safe Rust surface borrows a NUL-terminated string (static through set_str, or caller-kept through set_str_borrowed), never writes through it, and never frees it. The independent scalar fields do not bound the string or imply allocation. Unlike AVBPrint this is not self-referential and is freely copyable.'}}}})
cls=types['AVClass'];name=cls['fields'][-1]['ptr'].copy();name['borrowed']={'lifetime':'other'};name['note']='Usually a static literal in an immutable static class. Exception: libavfilter/vidstabutils.c:vs2av_log builds a stack-local class with class_name = tag borrowed from its caller, valid only during synchronous av_vlog. ClassRef and its string view must be bounded by the actual class/name lifetime, not assumed static. The wrapper accepts NULL names.'
submission('class-lifetime-not-always-static',{'_comment_agent':'Review core wave-1 batch-0: published library classes and child_class_iterate results are immutable static descriptors; no class-specific allocator, disposer, or cloner exists. Exception to the previous whole-tree static-only claim: libavfilter/vidstabutils.c:vs2av_log initializes an automatic AVClass with a borrowed caller tag and passes its address through a stack context to synchronous av_vlog. ClassRef must carry the actual descriptor and pointee lifetime. Class::new is Rust-owned immutable storage (local or static); its name is static. No lifecycle representation is missing.', 'fields':{'class_name':{'ptr':name}}})
bp=types['AVBPrint']['fields'][0]['ptr'].copy();bp['note']=bp['note'].replace('NULL only after av_bprint_finalize handed the allocation out.','NULL after av_bprint_finalize either hands the allocation out or releases it with av_freep when ret_str is NULL; inline storage is not cleared by finalization.')
submission('bprint-finalize-null-state',{'fields':{'str':{'ptr':bp}}})
write(pathlib.Path('wavefront/helper-is-not-a-print-buffer/README.md'),'''# The sizeof helper does not own AVBPrint storage
Affected base: "'`23dc07587c751c8f7c82729839a4b0065c66bb5f`.
The previous `ff_pad_helper_AVBPrint.str` block said `owned: true`,
`borrowed.lifetime: self`, `mutable: true`, and both `string` and `array`.
It inferred runtime ownership from a different type, `AVBPrint`.
Evidence: `FF_PAD_STRUCTURE` in `libavutil/bprint.h` uses the helper only
in `sizeof`; no bprint routine takes a helper pointer. `BPrintFields` is
copyable, never frees its string, and independently sets all scalar fields.
The previous record'"'s own comment acknowledged these facts but its structured
field still directed a consumer toward an owning/self-referential wrapper.
Resubmit "'`submission.json` with `wavefront ... query types --name
ff_pad_helper_AVBPrint --update submission.json`. The nullable string is a
borrow of external immutable storage in the authored Rust surface; there
is no C runtime ownership to mirror. No Rust ABI or lifecycle change.
'"''')
write(pathlib.Path('wavefront/class-lifetime-not-always-static/README.md'),'''# Not every AVClass or class name is static
Affected base: "'`23dc07587c751c8f7c82729839a4b0065c66bb5f`.
The previous AVClass comment claimed every in-tree instance was file-scope
static const, and `class_name` was always a static literal. At
`libavfilter/vidstabutils.c:vs2av_log`, an automatic `AVClass class` stores
the caller'"'s "'`tag` and is reached through an automatic `VS2AVLogCtx` during
`av_vlog`. Neither class nor name has a guaranteed static lifetime.
The optional vidstab TU is not enabled in the reusable hermetic build, but
is a concrete counterexample to the repo-wide finding. The wrapper already
uses `ClassRef<'"'a>"'` and returns `&'"'a CStr"'`; retain that correct design.
Resubmit `submission.json` for AVClass, using `other` for the name'"'s borrow
and documenting the common static case. No missing class destructor exists:
automatic storage expires normally and the tag remains borrowed.
''')
write(pathlib.Path('wavefront/bprint-finalize-null-state/README.md'),'''# Finalize can clear str without transferring it
Affected base: "'`23dc07587c751c8f7c82729839a4b0065c66bb5f`.
The AVBPrint.str finding said NULL occurs only when finalize hands the
allocation out. `libavutil/bprint.c:av_bprint_finalize` also calls
`av_freep(&buf->str)` for an allocated string when `ret_str == NULL`, freeing
and clearing the field. The structured nullable/ownership properties were
correct; fix the note via the accompanying submission. Inline storage is
not cleared by either finalize path. The existing Rust drop policy correctly
selects the NULL-output disposal path.
'"''')
write(pathlib.Path('misc/class-static-only-documentation/README.md'),'''# Class documentation overstated static lifetime
Affected base: "'`23dc07587c751c8f7c82729839a4b0065c66bb5f`.
Home: `crustify/rust/ffmpeg/libavutil/log.rs`, AVClass anchor/module docs.
The docs called every FFmpeg class static const and described Class only as
a static. `libavfilter/vidstabutils.c:vs2av_log` has an automatic class whose
name borrows its caller'"'s tag; "'`Class::new` can also safely construct a local
Rust value. Clarify immutable-while-borrowed versus static lifetime. The
existing lifetime-bounded handles are correct; retain Send/Sync because
borrows forbid mutation and class callbacks obey their contracts, not because
every descriptor must be static. Add a local-class/thread/reborrow public-API
test and an internal stack-descriptor/heap-name projection test.
'"''')
